# PostHog reverse proxy. `src/lib/posthog.ts` sets `api_host: "/pr/posthog"` so
# analytics traffic leaves as first-party requests to lunora.sh rather than to a
# known tracker host. These two rules are what make that path resolve in
# production — the matching `server.proxy` entry in `vite.config.ts` only exists
# in the dev server, so without them every capture() would fall through to the
# SSR catch-all and be dropped.
#
# Two rules, not one: posthog-js loads its remote config and toolbar bundles from
# the assets host and sends events to the ingestion host. Order matters — the
# `/static/*` rule must precede the catch-all. 200 = proxy (rewrite), not a
# redirect; a 30x would break the CORS preflight on ingestion POSTs.
#
# Region is EU, matching VITE_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST. On a US project these become
# us-assets.i.posthog.com / us.i.posthog.com.
/pr/posthog/static/*  https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com/static/:splat  200
/pr/posthog/*         https://eu.i.posthog.com/:splat                200
